{
  "surface": "scan",
  "route": "/scan",
  "notes": "The Scanner at 393 CSS px: the title, the card's viewfinder, the start control, the upload picker's box and its hint. `origin` is the title, because the page's frame and the app's frame are different heights and the design is the gaps between these boxes, not where the first one lands. The camera itself is a live MediaStream and no client can record it as evidence, so the states are the frame and the cards around it: `at-rest` (the camera not started), `denied` (the permission refused, the page's own sentence) and `result` (a decoded payload, the same fixture symbol both decoders read). The result state is recorded from the upload path: it is the page's real decode of the fixture, not a rendered mock. Widths of the buttons are left out because they are the run of their words; colours are left out because the raster proves them.",
  "states": [
    {
      "name": "at-rest",
      "origin": "title",
      "capture": "card",
      "elements": [
        {
          "name": "title",
          "web": {
            "selector": "[data-visual='title'] h1"
          },
          "app": {
            "tag": "scan-title"
          },
          "properties": ["top", "height", "fontSize", "fontWeight", "lineHeight"]
        },
        {
